{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9038-1",
  "summary": "gst-plugins-good1.0, gst-plugins-base1.0 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins did not properly handle\ncertain network streams. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause an application crash or execute arbitrary code. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-3083, CVE-2026-3085)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins incorrectly handled certain\nMatroska files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause an\napplication crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-39043)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins incorrectly handled certain\nWAV files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to make GStreamer\nGood Plugins crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-39044)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins incorrectly handled certain\nMP4 audio tracks. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause an\napplication crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-46470)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins incorrectly handled certain\nMP4 files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to make GStreamer Good\nPlugins crash, resulting in a denial of service, or obtain sensitive\ninformation. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 20.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 22.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-46471)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins incorrectly handled certain\nWavPack audio files. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause an\napplication crash, resulting in a denial of service, or execute arbitrary\ncode. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and\nUbuntu 20.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-53705)\n\nIt was discovered that GStreamer Good Plugins and GStreamer Base Plugins\nincorrectly handled certain network streams. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2026-111183)",
